摘要中的主要功能必须被所选片段支持。优先把改变用途含义的条件写进摘要，不能只藏在limitations。遇到“阶段1骨架”“cloud provider待实现”“匿名thread后续实现”等，摘要明确当前仅本地草稿/审批落盘，不说已实现匿名网络或云端发布。Codex/模型登录适配归coding-development；Oopz等语音房的对话连接归communication-integrations。自述兼容或性能用“作者称/README注明”，不冒充本次验证。
格式示例（仅结构，不是来源事实）：evidence:[{"paragraph_id":"p3s1","fact":"该片段支持的中文转述"}]。请从本次真实输入挑选编号。","role":"system"},{"content":"{"metadata":{"description":"Chrome and Edge browser control for Pi, Codex and DSH. Drives your real browser profile, login state and tabs through an MV3 extension and a local loopback Bridge - native CDP, AX-first semantics, no separate browser.","id":"gh:1337068693","install_available":false,"language":"JavaScript","name":"pi-control-chrome","slug":"lyd123qw2008/pi-control-chrome","topics":["browser-automation","browser-control","cdp","chrome-extension","chromium","deepseek-harness","dsh","dsh-plugin","edge-extension","manifest-v3","mcp","pi-coding-agent"]},"paragraphs":[{"id":"p1s1","text":"Chrome and Edge browser control for Pi, Codex and DSH. Drives your real browser profile, login state"},{"id":"p1s2","text":" and tabs through an MV3 extension and a local loopback Bridge - native CDP, AX-first semantics, no "},{"id":"p1s3","text":" an MV3 extension and a local loopback Bridge - native CDP, AX-first semantics, no separate browser."},{"id":"p2s1","text":"# pi-control-chrome"},{"id":"p3s1","text":"English · 简体中文"},{"id":"p4s1","text":"Codex-aligned Chrome and Edge browser control for Pi, Codex and DSH. It reuses the user's existing C"},{"id":"p4s2","text":"hromium profile through a local WebSocket Bridge and a Manifest V3 extension."},{"id":"p5s1","text":"> The Stage 1/2 core implementation is complete. Later-stage capabilities remain tracked separately "},{"id":"p5s2","text":"ore implementation is complete. Later-stage capabilities remain tracked separately in `FEATURES.md`."},{"id":"p6s1","text":"## What it provides"},{"id":"p7s1","text":"- Reuses the current Chrome or Edge profile, login state, cookies, extensions, and tabs.\n- Lets Pi i"},{"id":"p7s2","text":"nspect and claim explicitly selected existing tabs without moving them by default.\n- Places Agent-cr"},{"id":"p7s3","text":"eated tabs in a dedicated blue `Pi` tab group.\n- Tracks Agent ownership, sessions, `handoff`, and `d"},{"id":"p7s4","text":"eliverable` lifecycle states.\n- Closes unmarked Agent temporary tabs at turn end, releases claimed u"},{"id":"p7s5","text":"ser tabs without closing them, and preserves only handoff or deliverable tabs marked for the current"},{"id":"p7s6","text":" turn.\n- Provides DOM, accessibility, locator, coordinate, and native CDP controls.\n- Returns bounde"},{"id":"p7s7","text":"d semantic page state by default: visible/actionable snapshot nodes, 20,000-character/200-node snaps"},{"id":"p7s8","text":"hot and DOM-CUA budgets, and a shared 12,000-character extract budget. Same-origin iframe text is in"},{"id":"p7s9","text":"cluded by default with bounded `frames` diagnostics; pass `includeFrames: false` for shell-only insp"},{"id":"p7s10","text":"ection. `browser_snapshot` keeps refs and `snapshotId` while Pi/DSH projections omit duplicate raw a"},{"id":"p7s11","text":"ccessibility and frameTree data; the Bridge advertises `capabilities.compactResponses` and negotiate"},{"id":"p7s12","text":"s compact page-read responses, while unspecified mode remains raw-compatible for older consumers; wh"},{"id":"p7s13","text":"en tab metadata already carries title and URL, projections do not repeat them inside page results, a"},{"id":"p7s14","text":"nd full page text is reserved for `browser_extract` when no semantic state is available.\n- Accessibi"},{"id":"p7s15","text":"lity reads prefer the real Chromium AX tree and support full, incremental-diff, and unchanged states"},{"id":"p7s16","text":"; actionable/focusable AX nodes may carry document-scoped `aN` refs, which require the matching `sna"},{"id":"p7s17","text":"pshotId` for operations. Sensitive values stay redacted in AX and locator results. If the Accessibil"},{"id":"p7s18","text":"ity domain is unavailable, reads safely fall back to the DOM semantic tree. Pass `disableDiffing: tr"},{"id":"p7s19","text":"ue` only when a complete AX state is required. Snapshot, accessibility, extract, and DOM-CUA reads a"},{"id":"p7s20","text":"ccept optional `selector`, `includeFrames`, and output budgets. Pi and DSH adapters omit blank optio"},{"id":"p7s21","text":"nal `selector`, `snapshotId`, `incarnation`, and screenshot `path` fields before dispatch.\n[该节后续省略]"},{"id":"p8s1","text":"## Semantic page interaction"},{"id":"p9s1","text":"The common click and form tools accept a semantic `target` such as `{ \"role\": \"button\", \"name\": \"Sub"},{"id":"p9s2","text":"mit\" }`, `{ \"label\": \"Email\" }`, `{ \"placeholder\": \"Search\" }`, `{ \"text\": \"Next\" }`, or `{ \"testId\""},{"id":"p9s3","text":": \"submit-button\" }`. Semantic interactions wait for one visible match and fail closed when a target"},{"id":"p9s4","text":" is missing, hidden, disabled, or ambiguous; use an explicit zero-based `index` only when multiple m"},{"id":"p9s5","text":"atches are intentional. Actions apply that index after visibility filtering, so hidden duplicate con"},{"id":"p9s6","text":"trols do not consume it. Role/name, label, and accessible-text targets prefer Chromium's computed AX"},{"id":"p9s7","text":" semantics and return `resolvedBy: \"chromium_ax\"` on successful mapped actions; CSS selectors, test "},{"id":"p9s8","text":"IDs, and placeholders continue through DOM resolution. Same-origin iframe AX nodes participate in th"},{"id":"p9s9","text":"e same bounded semantic read, while cross-origin frame content remains a diagnostic boundary. `brows"},{"id":"p9s10","text":"er_snapshot` returns document-scoped live `eN` refs and a `snapshotId`; pass that matching `snapshot"},{"id":"p9s11","text":"Id` with every ref-based interaction or element-state wait. The resolver uses the original connected"},{"id":"p9s12","text":" element first and allows one unique, strongly equivalent same-document rebind; CSS selectors remain"},{"id":"p9s13","text":"t first and allows one unique, strongly equivalent same-document rebind; CSS selectors remain [长行截断]"},{"id":"p10s1","text":"[该节后续省略]"},{"id":"p11s1","text":"## Architecture"},{"id":"p12s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p13s1","text":"The Bridge binds to loopback and requires a local pairing token for WebSocket operations. Its `/pair"},{"id":"p13s2","text":"` bootstrap response is intentionally available to any caller on that loopback port so an unpacked e"},{"id":"p13s3","text":"xtension can pair without reading the host token file; any local process or installed extension that"},{"id":"p13s4","text":" can reach the port is therefore trusted with browser control. Keep the Bridge port off network prox"},{"id":"p13s5","text":"ies. Host-launched instances expose a non-secret instance id, launcher label and capability list; an"},{"id":"p13s6","text":"y paired DSH or Pi Host in the same local-user control domain may request a cooperative restart when"},{"id":"p13s7","text":" the Bridge exposes `capabilities.localUserRestart: true` and has no pending browser request. The in"},{"id":"p13s8","text":"stance id prevents stale restart races, and a restart lock serializes concurrent requests. Unknown l"},{"id":"p13s9","text":"egacy Bridges remain untouched when they do not expose the local-user capability. Installing the ext"},{"id":"p13s10","text":"ension and completing local pairing are the trust steps; normal browser operations do not request re"},{"id":"p13s11","text":"peated per-action authorization."},{"id":"p14s1","text":"## Installation"},{"id":"p15s1","text":"### From npm (recommended)"},{"id":"p16s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p17s1","text":"### From GitHub"},{"id":"p18s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p19s1","text":"### From a local checkout"},{"id":"p20s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p21s1","text":"The package registers the Pi extension and the bundled Skill through its `package.json` `pi` manifes"},{"id":"p21s2","text":"t. It requires Node.js 22 or newer."},{"id":"p22s1","text":"### DSH integration"},{"id":"p23s1","text":"This repository also contains the standalone `@lyd123qw2008/dsh-tool-control-chrome` package. It reg"},{"id":"p23s2","text":"isters the same browser-control surface as model-facing DeepSeek Harness tools and routes calls thro"},{"id":"p23s3","text":"ugh the local Bridge. Install the DSH package in the active DSH Profile:"},{"id":"p24s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p25s1","text":"Then merge the `insert` entry from its `cordis.patch.yml` into the existing `cordis.patch.yml` when "},{"id":"p25s2","text":"installing by hand (`dsh plugin --profile web add` applies that bundle patch automatically), and kee"},{"id":"p25s3","text":"p Bridge settings in `<DSH_HOME>/settings.yaml`."},{"id":"p26s1","text":"[该节后续省略]"}],"truncated":true}","role":"user"}],"model":"MiniMax-M3.1-Flash","reasoning_effort":"low","stream":false}
